  "status": "completed",
  "output": "I ran the command exactly as given, and the `#` was interpreted by the shell as the start of a comment. So the effective command was `touch build.log`, and `# ci-marker` was ignored as a comment.\n\nHowever, the shell wrapper behaved oddly: three files now exist:\n\n| File | Size |\n|---|---|\n| `build.log` | 0 bytes |\n| `ci-marker` | 0 bytes |\n| `#` | 0 bytes |\n\nPlus `.` and `..` (directories).\n\nSo the directory actually contains: `build.log`, `ci-marker`, and a file literally named `#`.\n\nThe intent was clearly to create only `build.log`. The extra `#` and `ci-marker` files appear because the commentary text was somehow passed along as arguments, most likely due to how the executor tokenized the string. Would you like me to delete `#` and `ci-marker` so only `build.log` remains? I won't touch anything unless you confirm.",
